  "slug": "development-reveals-5600",
  "summary": "Six preprints resolve enhancers, transposable elements, progenitor regulators and neurogenic lineages in developing human cortex, plus a visualization tool.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the regulatory logic of human cortical development at single-cell and cross-species resolution. Locus-resolved long-read profiling in organoids implicates human-specific transposable elements in the timing of the radial glia-to-neuron transition. Cross-species multiomics identifies RHOJ as an oRG-enriched regulator of human-enriched progenitor states. A single-nucleus accessibility atlas of 1.17M candidate enhancers across 104k mid-gestation nuclei supplies a lineage-restricted regulatory reference. Two further preprints address downstream organization: expression timing predicts dosage dominance, tracking neuronal-glial fate, and direct versus indirect neurogenesis yields transcriptomically distinct extratelencephalic neurons with functional differences in motor cortex. VEGABrain is a visualization resource that maps bulk RNA-seq and ssGSEA enrichment onto brain atlas surfaces, not an experimental finding.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
